BORROWED GRAVITY
Gravity exists only because it’s being corrected

FORMAT (LOCKED)
Duration: 25s
Max shot length: 2.0s (hard cap)
Average shot length: 1.2–1.6s
FPS: 48
Color: Black & white, low contrast
Grain: Constant, analog, alive
CORE LAW (UPDATED)

❌ No static frames
❌ No shots longer than 2s
❌ No visual “rests”

✅ Motion never resets between cuts
✅ Each cut interrupts motion, never resolves it
✅ Cuts feel like gravity corrections, not edits

CAMERA RULE (IMPORTANT)

Cuts are phase cuts, not angle changes.
The camera:
Is always already moving
Never “arrives” anywhere
Continues momentum through cuts

25s TEMPORAL STRUCTURE
(~15–18 shots total, all under 2s)

0.0–1.4s
Slow lateral drift past the strings.
They vibrate asynchronously.
Moon already rotating — no intro.

1.4–2.8s
Cut closer.
Moon surface slides subtly, like a skin shift.
Craters misalign.

2.8–4.2s
Cut low.
Pebbles crawl sideways across the ground.
One lifts upward.

4.2–5.6s
Cut behind the couple.
Their silhouettes sway microscopically, delayed from gravity.

5.6–7.1s
Cut tight on strings.
One slackens.
Another compensates too late.

7.1–8.5s
Cut wide.
Dust moves in three conflicting vectors.
Nothing agrees.

8.5–10.0s
Cut closer to moon edge.
Rotation accelerates slightly, then corrects.

10.0–11.6s
Cut ground-level.
Shadows lag behind their sources by a fraction.

11.6–13.1s
Cut mid-air.
Floating debris rotates slowly, never settling.

13.1–14.6s
Cut behind strings again.
Micro-oscillation continues, now out of phase.

14.6–16.1s
Cut oblique angle.
Camera drifts left, objects drift right.

16.1–17.6s
Cut closer to the moon’s face.
Surface texture subtly reorganizes.

17.6–19.0s
Cut wider.
Entire system breathes — nothing stops.

19.0–20.6s
Cut tight again.
A knot trembles, holds.

20.6–22.1s
Cut mid-motion.
Moon rotation slightly wrong now.

22.1–23.6s
Cut wider, but unstable.
All motions continue, phase-shifted.

23.6–25.0s
Cut before anything resolves.
Motion mid-correction.
Hard cut to black.

SOUND LOGIC (CUT-AWARE)
Low continuous hum (never resets on cuts)
Micro creaks that ignore edit points
Air tone persists through all shots
No hit points, no stingers
Silence exists only between micro-sounds

EMOTIONAL EFFECT
Motion replaces certainty
Cuts feel like failed stabilizations
The world keeps correcting itself
Love survives inside perpetual adjustment

Not calm.
Not chaos.
Perpetual imbalance, sustained.